WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.566 --> 00:00:04.507
- [Commander] Is that
dude just standing there

00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:06.615
between the trees good or bad?

00:00:06.615 --> 00:00:08.017
- Hey, I'm right by the mule.

00:00:08.017 --> 00:00:10.272
- Where are you in relation
to the burning car?

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:12.129
- [Christian] What we
do here is unorthodox.

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:14.363
We teach the art and the
science of leadership.

00:00:14.363 --> 00:00:16.407
- [Commander] Incoming, incoming.

00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:17.412
- Both eyes are open.

00:00:17.412 --> 00:00:18.315
Now we're gonna go.

00:00:18.315 --> 00:00:19.297
- My name is Christian.

00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:20.562
I'm a former Marine,

00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:23.545
and I am on an undisclosed military base.

00:00:23.545 --> 00:00:27.032
We conduct multi-day,
pseudo-military operations,

00:00:27.032 --> 00:00:29.371
with corporate executives and veterans,

00:00:29.371 --> 00:00:31.927
so that when we conclude these missions,

00:00:31.927 --> 00:00:34.369
the executives say, “Hey,
we need to hire a lot more

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:36.573
of these men and women.”

00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:38.854
We're gonna help organizations move better

00:00:38.854 --> 00:00:43.021
by doing something that's
also considered a social good.

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.863
- Right now, there's over
250,000 service members

00:00:50.863 --> 00:00:53.036
that transition out of
the service every year.

00:00:53.036 --> 00:00:54.310
My goal is to make sure

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.887
that no veteran goes
through the same situations

00:00:56.887 --> 00:00:58.344
that I had to go through.

00:00:58.344 --> 00:01:01.256
- Casey went from the
pinnacle of athleticism

00:01:01.256 --> 00:01:04.192
to someone who was carted
out of a dusty battlefield

00:01:04.192 --> 00:01:06.478
in Afghanistan, paralyzed.

00:01:06.478 --> 00:01:07.405
When he was recovering,

00:01:07.405 --> 00:01:09.453
he was told he was never gonna walk again.

00:01:09.453 --> 00:01:11.896
And he said, Well, no.

00:01:11.896 --> 00:01:13.116
And he persisted.

00:01:13.116 --> 00:01:17.261
After two years, he actually
walked out of the hospital.

00:01:17.261 --> 00:01:19.491
He was discharged just a
number of months later,

00:01:19.491 --> 00:01:21.901
and Casey, this war hero,
finds himself living out

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:24.065
of his car for a while.

00:01:24.065 --> 00:01:25.458
- I had just gotten out.

00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:26.749
I was one of those typical veterans,

00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:28.902
I was like, you know what, I got this.

00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:31.353
I'm gonna go out there; I have
all of these marketable skills,

00:01:31.353 --> 00:01:33.806
everybody's gonna wanna hire me.

00:01:33.806 --> 00:01:34.806
I was wrong.

00:01:35.644 --> 00:01:37.462
- [Christian] When our
veterans transition,

00:01:37.462 --> 00:01:40.359
out of the military, they
have to find the uniform

00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:42.844
that they're gonna wear
in their future career.

00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:45.671
- [Casey] My closet used to
be all camouflage uniforms.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.338
Now, I'm talking about pocket squares,

00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:49.094
and ties, and cuff links,

00:01:49.094 --> 00:01:49.993
but the thing is,

00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:51.356
is I love when I put on a suit.

00:01:51.356 --> 00:01:52.780
It makes me feel empowered,

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.310
and gives me a sense of
belonging with my peers now.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.657
I knew that I can get from
where I was in the military,

00:02:00.657 --> 00:02:02.088
I just needed the opportunity.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.667
Christian saw that within me.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.015
- You know, this is the,

00:02:06.015 --> 00:02:07.525
our last night together,

00:02:07.525 --> 00:02:09.968
and you've learned a lot.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.394
- Really more than anything,
you learn about people,

00:02:12.394 --> 00:02:14.095
and you learn about relationships,

00:02:14.095 --> 00:02:15.530
and how important that is.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.670
- What always comes to
my mind is how I live a,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.907
charmed life.

00:02:18.907 --> 00:02:21.360
Meeting you, dude, and your story, just,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.443
it just cuts to the bone.

00:02:25.193 --> 00:02:26.766
- What you guys are
doing for these veterans

00:02:26.766 --> 00:02:28.356
on a daily basis,

00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:29.779
you guys are my heroes.

00:02:29.779 --> 00:02:32.890
We are gonna change the
way that America looks

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:33.979
at hiring veterans,

00:02:33.979 --> 00:02:36.654
hiring a veteran as good business.

00:02:36.654 --> 00:02:38.816
- Life is simply bettered
if we're in service

00:02:38.816 --> 00:02:40.981
to something bigger than ourselves.

00:02:40.981 --> 00:02:43.742
What we do here is our
attempt to dent the universe.

00:02:43.742 --> 00:02:45.348
We're unsure whether
we'll dent the universe,

00:02:45.348 --> 00:02:48.515
but we're gonna swing like hell at it.

00:02:52.173 --> 00:02:54.756
(ambient tone)

